  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO Prize for Girls&apos; and Women&apos;s Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &apos;UNESCO Prize for girls&apos; and women&apos;s education&apos; was proposed by China, and adopted by 197EX/47 (Oct 2015). It was renewed for a second five- year cycle (2021 - 2025) at the 210Th Executive Board with continued support from China (see 210 EX/16.111). The Prize will be awarded annually to two prize winners who have made outstanding contributions in this field. The Prize, which consists of a monetary reward of US $50.000 for each of the two winners, will be given to individuals, institutions, other entities or non-governmental organizations actively engaged in identified priority areas. The Prize rewards in particular activities that are innovative and/or have a high impact.</narrative>
  </description>
